{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>The blessing, when you heed.</b> In the blessing he did not mention 'if you heed,' as he mentioned in the curse. And he said, 'and the curse, if you do not heed,' because that is language of uncertainty, and he did not wish to mention it in connection with the good; but in the calamity he did mention language of uncertainty. Therefore in the blessing he wrote אשר תשמעו — 'when you heed' — which is language of certainty."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:41.588751611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}